Let's find the slope between $\blueE{B(8,1)}$ and $\purpleD{C(1,-9)}$.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{\blueE{1}-(\purpleD{-9})}{\blueE{8}-\purpleD{1}}\\\\
&=\dfrac{10}{7}
\end{align}$

Next, let's find the slope between $\maroonD{A(2,7)}$ and $\goldE{D(-6,-2)}$.

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{\Delta y}{\Delta x} &= \dfrac{\maroonD{7}-(\goldE{-2})}{\maroonD{2}-(\goldE{-6})}\\\\
&=\dfrac{9}{8}
\end{align}$
